1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,406
In this lesson, we'll make
sense of your Kyntlo bill.

2
00:00:03,406 --> 00:00:06,751
You'll learn the difference
between your plan and your usage,

3
00:00:06,751 --> 00:00:11,192
how to read your wallet, and how to make
sure your calls and messages never stop.

4
00:00:12,062 --> 00:00:14,155
Open Settings, then Billing.

5
00:00:14,155 --> 00:00:15,950
Your bill has two parts.

6
00:00:15,950 --> 00:00:19,389
The first is your plan,
a fixed monthly price.

7
00:00:19,389 --> 00:00:22,678
Bloom is on Pro, at
$490 a month plus taxes.

8
00:00:22,678 --> 00:00:26,939
It covers all the features,
your users, and your hosting.

9
00:00:27,792 --> 00:00:33,055
The second part is usage: the emails,
texts and calls you actually send and make.

10
00:00:33,055 --> 00:00:35,135
These are paid from your wallet.

11
00:00:35,135 --> 00:00:36,889
Open Wallet & Transactions.

12
00:00:36,889 --> 00:00:41,633
Here's your current balance, and usage
is deducted from it as it happens.

13
00:00:42,483 --> 00:00:45,169
Below is your usage summary for the month.

14
00:00:45,169 --> 00:00:49,518
For each service, you see how much
you used, the rate, and the cost.

15
00:00:49,518 --> 00:00:52,972
These are wholesale rates,
with no markup from Kyntlo.

16
00:00:52,972 --> 00:00:56,106
You pay what the telecom
and AI providers charge.

17
00:00:56,954 --> 00:01:00,603
Email is very cheap: $0.00135 per email.

18
00:01:00,603 --> 00:01:05,255
Bloom's newsletter to 2,140
patients cost under $3.

19
00:01:05,255 --> 00:01:08,995
Texts are billed per segment, at $0.0158.

20
00:01:08,995 --> 00:01:15,106
One segment is up to 160 characters,
and emojis shorten that to 70,

21
00:01:15,106 --> 00:01:16,931
so keep texts short.

22
00:01:17,782 --> 00:01:23,768
Calls are billed per minute: $0.028 to
make a call, and $0.017 to receive one.

23
00:01:23,768 --> 00:01:28,834
And on Pro, AI usage is unlimited,
so Conversation AI, Content AI,

24
00:01:28,834 --> 00:01:32,211
Reviews AI and Workflow
AI show as included.

25
00:01:32,211 --> 00:01:36,662
On other plans, they're charged
at the rates you see here.

26
00:01:37,518 --> 00:01:39,317
To top up, click Add Balance.

27
00:01:39,317 --> 00:01:42,171
Choose an amount, check
the card, and confirm.

28
00:01:42,171 --> 00:01:44,404
The new balance shows straight away.

29
00:01:44,404 --> 00:01:47,754
Top-ups are charged to the
card saved on your account,

30
00:01:47,754 --> 00:01:50,483
and they appear in your
wallet transactions.

31
00:01:51,334 --> 00:01:54,044
Better still, switch on auto recharge.

32
00:01:54,044 --> 00:01:57,396
Here, whenever Bloom's
balance falls below $10,

33
00:01:57,396 --> 00:02:00,248
the wallet adds $40 from the saved card.

34
00:02:00,248 --> 00:02:06,025
That way, reminders, missed-call text-backs
and phone calls never stop because of

35
00:02:06,025 --> 00:02:07,166
an empty wallet.

36
00:02:08,016 --> 00:02:11,416
Wallet transactions lists
every top-up and usage charge,

37
00:02:11,416 --> 00:02:14,574
including the monthly rental
for your phone numbers,

38
00:02:14,574 --> 00:02:17,245
so you can see exactly
where the money went.

39
00:02:17,245 --> 00:02:20,524
And the Invoices tab keeps
your monthly plan invoices,

40
00:02:20,524 --> 00:02:22,832
ready to download for your accountant.

41
00:02:23,683 --> 00:02:24,749
Here's a pro tip.

42
00:02:24,749 --> 00:02:27,384
Glance at your usage summary once a month.

43
00:02:27,384 --> 00:02:32,340
If one line suddenly jumps, it's usually
a workflow sending more often than you

44
00:02:32,340 --> 00:02:35,162
meant, and it's an easy
fix once you spot it.

45
00:02:35,162 --> 00:02:37,923
Your execution logs
will show you which one.

46
00:02:38,775 --> 00:02:41,537
Now you know exactly
what you're paying for.

47
00:02:41,537 --> 00:02:46,558
In the last lesson of this module, we'll
cover data, privacy and do not disturb.

48
00:02:46,558 --> 00:02:47,437
See you there.
